=== task: predict easy
title: An out-of-date pair
prompt: This version prints a line each time a pair comes off the heap. What does it print?
code:
```python
import heapq

graph = {"S": [("A", 4), ("B", 1)], "A": [], "B": [("A", 1)]}
dist = {"S": 0, "A": float("inf"), "B": float("inf")}
heap = [(0, "S")]
done = set()
while heap:
    d, u = heapq.heappop(heap)
    if u in done:
        print("skip", d, u)
        continue
    done.add(u)
    print("settle", d, u)
